    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n49724" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰάσμη</span></b> , ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>jessamine, Jasminum
			officinale</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Aët.
			</span></i> ap. Ps.-<i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				1.63
			</span></i> (fr. <i><span class="en">
				Pers.
			</span></i>
			<i>yāsam</i>): <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰάσμῐνον</span></b> , τό, <i>oil of
				jasmine</i>, ibid.:—also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰασμέλαιον</span></b> , 
			τό, <i><span class="en">
				Aët.
				1.119
			</span></i> (who states that <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰάσμη</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰάσμινον</span>
			
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰασμέλαιον</span>
			 was prepared <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκ τῶν ἀνθῶν τῶν
				λευκῶν τοῦ ἴου, καὶ ἐλαίου σησαμίνου</span>).</div>
